GAL22V10
VJVCTRLR5

FETCH A11 A12 A13 A14 A15 MREQn RDn WRn MODE0 MODE1 GND
RESETn WAITn MUXSEL D245DIR /D245OE /FBCEn /FBWEn /FBOEn NC NC CPUACC VCC

; D800-FFFF belongs to video only in memory modes 0 and 3.  CPUACC is an
; internal-feedback macrocell; its physical pin is intentionally unconnected.
CPUACC = RESETn * /MREQn * A15 * A14 * A13 * /MODE1 * /MODE0 * /RDn
       + RESETn * /MREQn * A15 * A14 * A13 * /MODE1 * /MODE0 * /WRn
       + RESETn * /MREQn * A15 * A14 * A13 * MODE1 * MODE0 * /RDn
       + RESETn * /MREQn * A15 * A14 * A13 * MODE1 * MODE0 * /WRn
       + RESETn * /MREQn * A15 * A14 * /A13 * A12 * A11 * /MODE1 * /MODE0 * /RDn
       + RESETn * /MREQn * A15 * A14 * /A13 * A12 * A11 * /MODE1 * /MODE0 * /WRn
       + RESETn * /MREQn * A15 * A14 * /A13 * A12 * A11 * MODE1 * MODE0 * /RDn
       + RESETn * /MREQn * A15 * A14 * /A13 * A12 * A11 * MODE1 * MODE0 * /WRn

; Scanout owns address/data during FETCH.  A colliding CPU request pulls WAIT
; low through the GAL's open-drain output and resumes as FETCH falls.
MUXSEL = /FETCH + /RESETn
WAITn.T = GND
WAITn.E = CPUACC * FETCH

; 74HCT245 DIR: high is CPU A-side -> framebuffer B-side (write), low is read.
D245DIR = RDn
/D245OE = CPUACC * /FETCH

; SRAM controls are active-low.  Reset disables both owners; scan reads during
; FETCH, while CPU reads/writes are admitted only outside FETCH.
/FBCEn = RESETn * FETCH
       + CPUACC * /FETCH
/FBOEn = RESETn * FETCH
       + CPUACC * /FETCH * /RDn
/FBWEn = CPUACC * /FETCH * /WRn

DESCRIPTION

VJUGA rev B Video-card U7 framebuffer decode, arbitration and open-drain WAIT.
